Stage 03 names both kill chains: the same property, the page says, made them so hard to detect.
notes:
Two related kill chains on csoh.org, and the page's related defense topics.

Stage 03 names Storm-0558 and the Entra ID Actor token flaw. Replaying a session token skips the entire login path, with no sign-in event that looks like an attack, and the page says that is the same property that made those two so hard to detect. Here it arrived without any cryptography being broken: the tokens were simply lying in files people had uploaded voluntarily. The page draws no other connection between them.

The defense topics cover identity and access management in the cloud, SaaS security and SaaS security posture management, detection engineering, and zero trust.
